# Knowledge base conventions

When working in a KB Genie knowledge base:

- Never modify files under `raw/`. Those originals are immutable.
- Write processed output only to `markdown/`, `summaries/`, `chunks/`, `concepts/`, `graphs/`, `logs/`, `tasks/`, and `index.yaml`.
- Treat `index.yaml` as the authoritative catalog. After adding or changing processed documents, keep it in sync via `kb-indexer`.
- Preserve required frontmatter schemas for summaries, chunks, and concept pages.
- Every chunk needs a non-empty `summary`, `semantic_key`, and at least one `potential_question`.
- Every concept page needs a Definition section and at least one source citation.
- Every document summary needs a non-empty `relevance_to_software` field.
- Prefer heading-boundary semantic chunks over arbitrary token splits.
